# Scoped deliberately: this file governs docs/skill-backups/ ONLY.
#
# A repo-wide .gitattributes was logged as "ready" in commit d837382 but is not
# on disk. This is NOT that file and does not attempt to be — this repo is
# mixed on purpose (api/sd-data.js is stored CRLF, sairncare.html LF), so a
# blanket rule would rewrite real source files. Adding one is still open work
# for whoever owns that decision.
#
# WHY THIS RULE EXISTS
# docs/skill-backups/ is a byte-exact disaster-recovery archive of 29 skills
# that exist nowhere else. This repo runs core.autocrlf=true with no
# .gitattributes, so Git would convert those files' LF endings to CRLF on
# checkout. A restored archive would then differ byte-for-byte from what was
# backed up — silently, and only visible at the moment you most need it to be
# correct. `-text` disables all end-of-line conversion in both directions, so
# what is committed is what is restored.
docs/skill-backups/** -text
